1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,100
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,100
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:03,133
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,133 --> 00:00:06,133
[Episode 3]

5
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:08,926
- Hello, sir.
- Yeah.

6
00:00:20,296 --> 00:00:22,248
You're going to stare a hole through it.

7
00:00:22,248 --> 00:00:24,264
I won't test you, so take it easy.

8
00:00:24,264 --> 00:00:26,857
It's going to be a long haul,
so brace yourself.

9
00:00:26,857 --> 00:00:28,464
Sir, this...

10
00:00:28,464 --> 00:00:30,716
What, what is it?

11
00:00:33,108 --> 00:00:34,683
[Incident Report]
Oh, that case.

12
00:00:34,683 --> 00:00:35,884
The case where a dad was murdered
on Christmas night,

13
00:00:35,884 --> 00:00:37,349
right in front of his daughter.

14
00:00:37,349 --> 00:00:39,049
"He abused his wife and child,

15
00:00:39,049 --> 00:00:41,484
and eventually stabbed his wife
to death with a soju bottle."

16
00:00:41,484 --> 00:00:45,821
"Then, seven years after his release,
he tried to kill his daughter?"

17
00:00:45,821 --> 00:00:48,085
The part about the daughter
was never made public.

18
00:00:48,085 --> 00:00:50,680
She was still a minor at the time,

19
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:54,340
and she may have been a witness.

20
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:55,483
A witness?

21
00:00:55,483 --> 00:00:57,084
She saw Kingfisher?

22
00:00:57,084 --> 00:01:01,316
If she had, do you think
we'd still have zero leads?

23
00:01:02,916 --> 00:01:04,664
Well, you never know.

24
00:01:04,664 --> 00:01:08,790
Maybe she really didn't see anything,
or maybe she's keeping quiet.

25
00:01:08,790 --> 00:01:12,716
Oh, the daughter's name was 'Oh' something.

26
00:01:24,095 --> 00:01:25,516
Are you crazy?

27
00:01:25,516 --> 00:01:27,316
What are you...

28
00:01:27,968 --> 00:01:30,800
So you really don't want me to die, do you?

29
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,383
The only witness to
one of Kingfisher's shootings.

30
00:01:35,383 --> 00:01:38,549
The only child I ever revealed myself to.

31
00:01:40,536 --> 00:01:43,083
It's been a while, Oh Seung Ah.

32
00:01:57,532 --> 00:02:00,268
Merry Christmas, Yoo Bo Na!

33
00:02:00,268 --> 00:02:01,392
Where's my present?

34
00:02:01,392 --> 00:02:04,564
Santa Claus will bring you one.

35
00:02:04,564 --> 00:02:05,924
Yeah, right. Like he'd ever do that.

36
00:02:05,924 --> 00:02:06,924
You never know.

37
00:02:06,924 --> 00:02:09,368
He's said to have a very clear
sense of right and wrong.

38
00:02:09,368 --> 00:02:11,020
I don't think he's got
a present for you either.

39
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:13,208
You're a terrible boss for making me
work on a day like this.

40
00:02:13,208 --> 00:02:15,083
It's not like you've got plans.

41
00:02:15,083 --> 00:02:17,724
Do you have friends? A partner? Family?

42
00:02:17,724 --> 00:02:20,252
Yet here you are, all by yourself.

43
00:02:20,252 --> 00:02:23,860
But it's all romance comics, huh?

44
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:25,148
Seeing someone these days?

45
00:02:25,148 --> 00:02:27,752
Go home early. Kids are waiting.

46
00:02:27,752 --> 00:02:29,964
Will a punk who's meant to die not die
just because you delay it a few days?

47
00:02:29,964 --> 00:02:34,149
He might kill someone first.

48
00:02:39,992 --> 00:02:42,283
But isn't it possible he's changed?

49
00:02:42,283 --> 00:02:43,683
Still, he's her dad.

50
00:02:43,683 --> 00:02:48,683
I know, questioning one more time
and never giving up hope until the end.

51
00:02:48,683 --> 00:02:50,924
That's how you do things.

52
00:02:50,924 --> 00:02:53,348
If you want to watch a little longer, do it.

53
00:02:53,348 --> 00:02:57,316
Just don't miss your chance.

54
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:02,024
It's cold. Take some hand warmers.

55
00:03:02,024 --> 00:03:04,183
I'm off.

56
00:03:07,842 --> 00:03:10,074
[Oh Seung Ah's Daily Route]

57
00:03:30,347 --> 00:03:33,544
<i>I thought, "That day
would be the last day of my life."</i>

58
00:03:33,544 --> 00:03:38,049
<i>"It would be my last Christmas."</i>

59
00:03:39,564 --> 00:03:42,449
<i>I thought I'd never see this again.</i>

60
00:03:43,184 --> 00:03:47,348
<i>Whether I died or killed him.</i>

61
00:03:48,836 --> 00:03:52,452
<i>Right, that's probably why.</i>

62
00:03:52,452 --> 00:03:54,416
<i>I heard your heart.</i>

63
00:04:02,312 --> 00:04:04,949
Do you want a Christmas present?

64
00:04:08,352 --> 00:04:10,799
Then no crying.

65
00:04:10,799 --> 00:04:12,983
You have to be good.

66
00:04:13,752 --> 00:04:17,816
I heard that Santa is very clear
about right and wrong.

67
00:04:17,816 --> 00:04:19,372
Miss, who are you?

68
00:04:19,372 --> 00:04:23,749
Leave the living room window
slightly open when you get home.

69
00:04:29,964 --> 00:04:31,683
See you again.

70
00:04:34,312 --> 00:04:37,420
<i>Assistant Manager Yoo Bo Na,
what on earth are you doing?</i>

71
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:40,216
<i>Why would you reveal your face like that?</i>

72
00:04:48,084 --> 00:04:50,283
Does she think she's Santa or something?

73
00:04:50,928 --> 00:04:54,016
She doesn't even know what I wished for.

74
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:14,503
<i>I prayed to just let me die quickly instead.</i>

75
00:05:14,503 --> 00:05:18,983
<i>If God existed, I begged Him
to save me from hell.</i>

76
00:05:18,983 --> 00:05:21,049
<i>Right at that moment...</i>

77
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:32,849
<i>God really appeared.</i>

78
00:05:46,348 --> 00:05:48,283
<i>The reason I came back.</i>

79
00:05:49,416 --> 00:05:52,749
<i>The reason I do this.</i>

80
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:56,716
<i>Hoping to save even just one person.</i>

81
00:05:57,500 --> 00:06:01,983
<i>Hoping that because of this work,
someone might be safe.</i>

82
00:06:04,512 --> 00:06:06,283
You knew all along.

83
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:10,549
You knew everything
from the start, but why...

84
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:14,349
Because I was disappointed.

85
00:06:15,316 --> 00:06:20,392
I just wanted that child to be happy

86
00:06:20,392 --> 00:06:22,980
and live a normal life like everyone else,

87
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:24,649
but that wasn't how things turned out.

88
00:06:25,816 --> 00:06:28,583
I didn't like your choice.

89
00:06:30,716 --> 00:06:32,449
I...

90
00:06:34,749 --> 00:06:37,749
I wanted to be like you.

91
00:06:38,649 --> 00:06:42,549
I wanted to stand beside you someday,

92
00:06:42,549 --> 00:06:46,716
so I've been working myself to death
until now with just that one dream.

93
00:06:50,249 --> 00:06:52,292
You shouldn't have.

94
00:06:52,292 --> 00:06:54,728
You should've followed your own path.

95
00:06:54,728 --> 00:06:57,049
A safe, bright one.

96
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:06,616
You told me we'd meet again.

97
00:07:08,484 --> 00:07:10,208
What?

98
00:07:13,789 --> 00:07:15,264
See you again.

99
00:07:15,264 --> 00:07:18,749
No, I just meant I hoped you'd stay safe...

100
00:07:18,749 --> 00:07:22,472
I don't know about that,
but anyway, take responsibility.

101
00:07:22,472 --> 00:07:23,924
Me?

102
00:07:23,924 --> 00:07:26,149
You're still such a kid, huh?

103
00:07:27,772 --> 00:07:29,549
What are you?

104
00:07:31,692 --> 00:07:34,483
It was the gift I had desperately wished for.

105
00:07:35,268 --> 00:07:37,584
<i>You were my Santa,</i>

106
00:07:37,584 --> 00:07:39,716
the savior of my life.

107
00:07:42,349 --> 00:07:44,576
So take responsibility.

108
00:07:44,576 --> 00:07:48,020
And yet you drugged my husband?

109
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:50,824
It wasn't poison. Just a sleeping pill.

110
00:07:50,824 --> 00:07:53,149
Would Kingfisher fall for
something like that?

111
00:07:53,149 --> 00:07:56,016
I know it was a sleeping pill, okay?

112
00:07:56,016 --> 00:07:57,916
Then why bring a gun?

113
00:07:57,916 --> 00:07:59,804
The bullets were real too.

114
00:07:59,804 --> 00:08:01,620
You actually fired it!

115
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:05,749
Because you messed with someone
you never should have.

116
00:08:11,148 --> 00:08:13,449
What an idiot...

117
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:29,983
You've really been working hard, huh?

118
00:08:31,824 --> 00:08:33,916
So it was from this point on?

119
00:08:39,888 --> 00:08:42,916
You didn't like my choice either?

120
00:08:42,916 --> 00:08:44,316
About six years ago...

121
00:08:44,316 --> 00:08:47,616
[Six Years Ago]

122
00:08:51,264 --> 00:08:52,516
<i>I saw you by chance.</i>

123
00:08:52,516 --> 00:08:54,044
Honey!

124
00:08:54,044 --> 00:08:56,483
<i>I recognized you instantly.</i>

125
00:08:57,156 --> 00:09:00,116
<i>Because I never forgot you
for a single day after that.</i>

126
00:09:07,476 --> 00:09:11,228
<i>It felt like there was a hole in my chest.</i>

127
00:09:11,228 --> 00:09:13,864
<i>The woman who'd been my god and heroine</i>

128
00:09:13,864 --> 00:09:17,356
<i>had become just an ordinary, fragile person.</i>

129
00:09:17,356 --> 00:09:19,483
So you're more like an anti-fan.

130
00:09:21,883 --> 00:09:24,168
So?

131
00:09:24,168 --> 00:09:25,748
I want to bring you back.

132
00:09:25,748 --> 00:09:28,916
Back to the old Kingfisher,
the woman I used to know.

133
00:09:30,216 --> 00:09:31,732
So you're an idiot after all.

134
00:09:31,732 --> 00:09:33,420
I think I told you.

135
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:36,852
You made your choice, and I respected it.

136
00:09:36,852 --> 00:09:39,800
Even if I didn't like it, it was your life.

137
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,504
I only did what I had to do.

138
00:09:41,504 --> 00:09:44,449
How you live with it afterward is up to you.

139
00:09:44,449 --> 00:09:46,749
But Kingfisher...

140
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:50,656
You seem to be mistaken about something.

141
00:09:50,656 --> 00:09:53,349
If I were your savior,

142
00:09:53,349 --> 00:09:56,516
the man who saved Kingfisher
was Kwon Tae Seong.

143
00:09:57,572 --> 00:09:59,312
It was him.

144
00:10:01,092 --> 00:10:02,883
That guy...

145
00:10:03,748 --> 00:10:06,664
saved your life?

146
00:10:06,664 --> 00:10:08,583
He saved something even greater.

147
00:10:11,176 --> 00:10:13,549
I received an even greater gift.

148
00:10:34,296 --> 00:10:36,916
It's Yoo Bo Na!

149
00:10:37,744 --> 00:10:40,100
Honey, do you know where we are now?

150
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:42,283
A cafe...

151
00:10:44,549 --> 00:10:47,578
Never thought I'd get a call telling me
to pick up my husband from a cafe

152
00:10:47,578 --> 00:10:51,352
because it was closing.

153
00:10:51,352 --> 00:10:53,732
What is going on?

154
00:10:53,732 --> 00:10:55,849
Oh, my!

155
00:10:57,056 --> 00:10:59,883
Did I fall asleep? What? Why?

156
00:11:01,692 --> 00:11:04,216
But when did I fall asleep?

157
00:11:08,020 --> 00:11:09,720
It's nighttime already!

158
00:11:13,584 --> 00:11:15,696
Our date...

159
00:11:15,696 --> 00:11:17,192
Well, it's all over for today.

160
00:11:17,192 --> 00:11:19,349
What are you going to do about this?

161
00:11:22,157 --> 00:11:24,440
I'm sorry. I'll...

162
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:27,949
I'll do the dishes for a month.
I'm really sorry.

163
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:31,949
You think that'll make up for it?

164
00:11:35,084 --> 00:11:36,556
No?

165
00:11:36,556 --> 00:11:40,112
I'll also take Yul to daycare
every morning for a month.

166
00:11:40,112 --> 00:11:41,944
I'm really sorry.

167
00:11:41,944 --> 00:11:43,960
Okay, I'll accept that.

168
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:49,748
And you'll read Yul a bedtime story
every night for a month.

169
00:11:49,748 --> 00:11:51,460
Okay, okay. Deal.

170
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,728
- Okay?
- Yeah.

171
00:11:52,728 --> 00:11:54,812
- Good.
- I'm really sorry.

172
00:11:54,812 --> 00:11:56,400
I ruined our precious time together.

173
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:59,849
Really, I'll really make it up to you.
Double, I'll really make it up double.

174
00:12:02,532 --> 00:12:03,532
What are we going to do about this?

175
00:12:03,532 --> 00:12:05,783
Honey, I'm so embarrassed.
Let's get out of here.

176
00:12:05,783 --> 00:12:08,883
Se Ah keeps calling. Get up, now.

177
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,188
Are you okay?

178
00:12:11,188 --> 00:12:13,093
- I'm okay.
- Can you walk?

179
00:12:13,093 --> 00:12:14,793
Yeah.

180
00:12:16,712 --> 00:12:22,016
If what I fed him was really poison,
I'd have died by your hand, right?

181
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:24,520
Director.

182
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:28,749
If you get caught calling me like that
at work too, seriously...

183
00:12:29,528 --> 00:12:31,449
you're really going to die, okay?

184
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,972
At work too...

185
00:12:35,972 --> 00:12:39,083
At work too...

186
00:12:41,083 --> 00:12:43,449
See you at work?

187
00:13:06,849 --> 00:13:11,283
<i>Is family really worth risking your life for?</i>

188
00:13:11,283 --> 00:13:14,149
- Heave-ho!
- Wow!

189
00:13:14,984 --> 00:13:16,683
Mom, I'm hungry.

190
00:13:16,683 --> 00:13:18,112
Yul, are you hungry?

191
00:13:18,112 --> 00:13:19,948
It's time for Yul to eat, isn't it?

192
00:13:19,948 --> 00:13:21,840
Since we're already out,
should we eat out before going home?

193
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,796
Honey, your mom's radish kimchi
is perfectly fermented.

194
00:13:23,796 --> 00:13:25,744
It's because I thought you might be tired.

195
00:13:25,744 --> 00:13:26,949
You said that because
you were worried I'd be tired?

196
00:13:26,949 --> 00:13:28,627
Yeah.

197
00:13:28,627 --> 00:13:30,780
Honey, look at the flowers.
Aren't they pretty?

198
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:32,116
- You're prettier.
- Really?

199
00:13:32,116 --> 00:13:34,460
- Yeah.
- Is Mommy prettier than flowers?

200
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:36,683
- Yeah!
- Really?

201
00:13:37,508 --> 00:13:39,583
<i>That was the wrong question.</i>

202
00:13:40,384 --> 00:13:42,620
<i>It's not about risking my life.</i>

203
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:45,649
<i>My family is my life.</i>

204
00:13:54,644 --> 00:13:57,820
So in the end, he saved one person.

205
00:13:57,820 --> 00:14:01,379
That girl would have died
if it weren't for Kingfisher, right?

206
00:14:01,379 --> 00:14:04,449
So, the conclusion is...

207
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:07,676
Man, that's just incredible!

208
00:14:07,676 --> 00:14:10,749
That's why he has over a million fans!

209
00:14:11,548 --> 00:14:13,672
Hey, aren't you going to snap out of it?

210
00:14:13,672 --> 00:14:15,583
Is that something a detective should say?

211
00:14:16,572 --> 00:14:18,272
I'm sorry, sir!

212
00:14:18,949 --> 00:14:23,549
Hey, all the victims killed
by Kingfisher were criminals.

213
00:14:23,549 --> 00:14:26,816
But does that justify murder?

214
00:14:26,816 --> 00:14:29,508
- No, it doesn't.
- The law is a social contract.

215
00:14:29,508 --> 00:14:30,772
Does he have the right

216
00:14:30,772 --> 00:14:34,198
to break that contract
and personally judge someone?

217
00:14:34,198 --> 00:14:35,349
- No, he doesn't!
- Should we,

218
00:14:35,349 --> 00:14:37,473
as police officers,
catch someone like that or not?

219
00:14:37,473 --> 00:14:39,916
- We should.
- How?

220
00:14:42,324 --> 00:14:44,412
Well?

221
00:14:44,412 --> 00:14:47,383
That's the conclusion. Got it?

222
00:14:50,856 --> 00:14:53,549
Let's get it together! Get it together!

223
00:14:55,036 --> 00:14:56,416
Here.

224
00:14:56,416 --> 00:14:58,272
Thank you.

225
00:14:58,272 --> 00:14:59,616
Dig through the files all the way.

226
00:14:59,616 --> 00:15:01,516
Up to the final case four years ago.

227
00:15:01,516 --> 00:15:05,283
You'll see another side of Kingfisher.

228
00:15:19,908 --> 00:15:23,083
Hey, don't go too deep.

229
00:15:23,083 --> 00:15:24,583
You might run into snakes.

230
00:15:24,583 --> 00:15:28,749
You have to dig deep to find anything.

231
00:15:30,008 --> 00:15:36,783
The good ones are always
the ones that stay hidden.

232
00:15:45,064 --> 00:15:46,884
What? What's that?

233
00:15:46,884 --> 00:15:49,349
- Is that a snake?
- Over there...

234
00:15:49,349 --> 00:15:51,449
Oh, my...

235
00:15:53,683 --> 00:15:55,916
[Not Today]

236
00:15:55,916 --> 00:15:58,549
[Social Affairs Desk]

237
00:15:59,404 --> 00:16:01,616
[Caller ID Restricted:
I'd like to provide a tip about Kingfisher]

238
00:16:02,452 --> 00:16:05,483
Well, did anyone come by while I was asleep?

239
00:16:05,483 --> 00:16:07,908
Someone who came while you were sleeping?

240
00:16:07,908 --> 00:16:09,104
Yeah.

241
00:16:09,104 --> 00:16:12,683
Well, I don't think I saw anyone.

242
00:16:14,538 --> 00:16:16,205
A tip about Kingfisher?

243
00:16:16,205 --> 00:16:17,603
You scared me!

244
00:16:17,603 --> 00:16:19,588
Jeez, stop popping up
from behind me like that.

245
00:16:19,588 --> 00:16:22,469
My colleague Kwon Tae Seong!

246
00:16:22,469 --> 00:16:23,660
Jeez...

247
00:16:23,660 --> 00:16:25,249
So you finally latched onto
the Kingfisher case, huh?

248
00:16:25,249 --> 00:16:26,483
I knew it.

249
00:16:26,483 --> 00:16:29,283
A swallow can't just pass by a mill, right?

250
00:16:31,852 --> 00:16:34,028
It's a sparrow, not a swallow.

251
00:16:34,028 --> 00:16:37,548
I was going to take it and pass it
to the right person if it was worth pursuing.

252
00:16:37,548 --> 00:16:38,683
What is it?

253
00:16:38,683 --> 00:16:40,244
What is it? What is it?

254
00:16:40,244 --> 00:16:42,214
Is it huge? A scoop?

255
00:16:42,214 --> 00:16:44,783
Did that person really not come?

256
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:48,249
Or did they come but fail to meet?

257
00:16:48,883 --> 00:16:50,816
There's been no contact since then.

258
00:16:50,816 --> 00:16:53,030
Was it just a prank?

259
00:16:53,030 --> 00:16:54,816
What are you talking about?

260
00:16:56,716 --> 00:17:01,316
But why does my colleague
and economics reporter, Go Ji Soon,

261
00:17:02,144 --> 00:17:05,649
always slack off instead of doing his job?

262
00:17:07,624 --> 00:17:10,612
You got stood up, huh? You got stood up.

263
00:17:10,612 --> 00:17:14,136
Man, how can you talk about
being stood up by a source

264
00:17:14,136 --> 00:17:16,649
and make it sound like
an editor-in-chief's report?

265
00:17:17,384 --> 00:17:19,338
Get out of here, you punk!

266
00:17:19,338 --> 00:17:20,912
Keep your chin up, okay?

267
00:17:20,912 --> 00:17:22,612
Fighting!

268
00:17:24,676 --> 00:17:27,548
Hello! Good morning!

269
00:17:27,548 --> 00:17:28,596
Hello.

270
00:17:28,596 --> 00:17:30,492
- Good morning.
- She's so cheerful, isn't she?

271
00:17:30,492 --> 00:17:31,724
- Hello!
- Good morning.

272
00:17:31,724 --> 00:17:34,446
She has no idea
what kind of person her senior is,

273
00:17:34,446 --> 00:17:36,649
and she's still that cheerful.

274
00:17:40,256 --> 00:17:44,512
- Hi.
- Good day. Hello.

275
00:17:44,512 --> 00:17:45,544
Mr. Tae Seong!

276
00:17:45,544 --> 00:17:49,366
I didn't know what you liked,
so I brought one of everything.

277
00:17:49,366 --> 00:17:51,575
Have whichever one you feel like.

278
00:17:51,575 --> 00:17:54,116
I'll take this one. Thank you, Ms. Hae Na.

279
00:17:55,108 --> 00:17:58,249
I already have my usual drink, so I'm fine.

280
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:03,579
That's not good...

281
00:18:03,579 --> 00:18:04,983
I'll enjoy it then, Ms. Hae Na.

282
00:18:04,983 --> 00:18:07,220
Wow, Mr. Kwon is so lucky.

283
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:08,284
Thank you, Ms. Hae Na.

284
00:18:08,284 --> 00:18:09,284
Ms. Hae Na, thank you.

285
00:18:09,284 --> 00:18:11,649
There's no one like you, Ms. Hae Na.

286
00:18:24,029 --> 00:18:25,729
Ms. Gu Hae Na.

287
00:18:26,995 --> 00:18:28,552
- Yes!
- Here...

288
00:18:28,552 --> 00:18:31,452
I organized some potential stories
we could look into.

289
00:18:31,452 --> 00:18:34,356
Take a look and let me know
if anything interests you.

290
00:18:34,356 --> 00:18:35,700
- Sorry?
- Oh.

291
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:38,149
We focus more on in-depth reports
than straight news,

292
00:18:38,149 --> 00:18:39,383
so our investigations take longer.

293
00:18:39,383 --> 00:18:42,749
We'll work on the reporting together
and split the articles.

294
00:18:43,383 --> 00:18:45,349
Yes, sir.

295
00:18:46,683 --> 00:18:48,404
[Managing Child Sex Offenders After Release]
A reporter's job is to prove themselves

296
00:18:48,404 --> 00:18:51,872
through their reporting
and articles above all else.

297
00:18:51,872 --> 00:18:53,572
You know that, right?

298
00:19:01,868 --> 00:19:05,708
What is this? What is this
mysterious character who walks the line

299
00:19:05,708 --> 00:19:07,683
between coldness and passion?

300
00:19:09,183 --> 00:19:11,183
[On-site Inspections
of the Serious Accidents Punishment Act]

301
00:19:11,183 --> 00:19:13,216
[Prison Overcrowding and Parole]

302
00:19:13,216 --> 00:19:14,816
[Voice Phishing Investigations:
Challenges and Solutions]

303
00:19:14,816 --> 00:19:17,940
A reporter who used to dig deeply
into a case or a person

304
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:20,704
suddenly dropped everything.

305
00:19:20,704 --> 00:19:22,684
That leaves only two possibilities.

306
00:19:22,684 --> 00:19:25,883
They were either paid off or threatened.

307
00:19:27,413 --> 00:19:30,854
Who got what?

308
00:19:30,854 --> 00:19:33,449
Oh, if it were me, I'd take the money.

309
00:19:33,449 --> 00:19:37,183
But he's the type neither of those
would work on.

310
00:19:44,052 --> 00:19:46,140
[Kingfisher Investigation Stalls]
But I feel like the spark

311
00:19:46,140 --> 00:19:48,416
[Identity Unknown]
has not gone out yet.

312
00:19:48,416 --> 00:19:50,749
[Durumi Electronics]

313
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:56,849
Hello!

314
00:19:56,849 --> 00:19:59,049
[Sales Team 3]

315
00:20:00,316 --> 00:20:02,404
[Team Leader Kim Bong Pal]

316
00:20:02,404 --> 00:20:04,816
- Good morning.
- Thank you, morning candy.

317
00:20:04,816 --> 00:20:05,816
Thank you.

318
00:20:05,816 --> 00:20:07,140
Good morning.

319
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:08,151
Thank you.

320
00:20:08,151 --> 00:20:10,449
- Good morning!
- Hello.

321
00:20:30,416 --> 00:20:31,983
[Client Report]

322
00:20:31,983 --> 00:20:32,983
Gold.

323
00:20:32,983 --> 00:20:35,016
[Gold: Above the Law Through Money and Power]

324
00:20:35,016 --> 00:20:36,016
White.

325
00:20:36,016 --> 00:20:37,513
[White: Offenders Against
Children and Adolescents]

326
00:20:37,513 --> 00:20:39,216
[Black: Murdered Two or More People]
Black.

327
00:20:39,216 --> 00:20:40,949
[Gray: Pre-Meeting Investigation Subjects]
Gray.

328
00:20:41,712 --> 00:20:43,412
Finish!

329
00:20:53,620 --> 00:20:55,188
I knew you would come, Mr. Lee.

330
00:20:55,188 --> 00:20:56,732
Oh, yeah.

331
00:20:56,732 --> 00:20:59,064
So you got picked
because of your track record.

332
00:20:59,684 --> 00:21:00,992
Oh, my.

333
00:21:00,992 --> 00:21:02,156
Thanks for your hard work.

334
00:21:02,156 --> 00:21:03,968
Track record? What track record?

335
00:21:03,968 --> 00:21:05,540
You didn't know?

336
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:08,720
Five years ago, taking down
the entire Oh Sun Il gang.

337
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,232
That was Mr. Lee's work.

338
00:21:10,232 --> 00:21:11,660
Oh, that huge case back then!

339
00:21:11,660 --> 00:21:13,112
Amazing!

340
00:21:13,112 --> 00:21:15,604
Oh, so that's why the Chief...

341
00:21:15,604 --> 00:21:18,004
Nothing this time either?

342
00:21:18,004 --> 00:21:20,236
No, nothing.

343
00:21:20,236 --> 00:21:23,564
They took the lungs, kidneys,
liver, and pancreas.

344
00:21:23,564 --> 00:21:25,449
They took everything.

345
00:21:25,449 --> 00:21:29,749
Judging by the rate of decomposition,
it's been about three or four weeks.

346
00:21:29,749 --> 00:21:35,183
Well, it may have been buried in winter
and decomposed as the weather warmed.

347
00:21:36,499 --> 00:21:39,652
It's been quiet for a while.
Thought it was over.

348
00:21:39,652 --> 00:21:41,844
Honestly, even in the middle of
all that chaos,

349
00:21:41,844 --> 00:21:44,396
they still roughly stitched it up
and dumped it.

350
00:21:44,396 --> 00:21:47,316
They're not fooling around.

351
00:21:47,316 --> 00:21:50,760
They seem even more ruthless
than the last ones.

352
00:21:50,760 --> 00:21:54,449
Mr. Lee, you're going to
have a tough time this time.

353
00:21:59,872 --> 00:22:02,196
[National Forensic Service]
Beom, what is the first thing to do?

354
00:22:02,196 --> 00:22:05,749
Since the victim was reported missing
while hiking on Mount Taegong,

355
00:22:05,749 --> 00:22:07,816
I'll check with the station in charge
about the investigation at the time.

356
00:22:07,816 --> 00:22:08,816
Look into it.

357
00:22:08,816 --> 00:22:11,288
Secure the CCTV footage
from the hiking trail back then too.

358
00:22:11,288 --> 00:22:13,812
Okay. I'll request help with
inquiries around Mount Cheongri,

359
00:22:13,812 --> 00:22:15,495
where the body was found.

360
00:22:15,495 --> 00:22:17,383
Hey, Beom.

361
00:22:17,383 --> 00:22:18,583
You look excited?

362
00:22:18,583 --> 00:22:20,064
[Forensic Imaging Room]

363
00:22:20,064 --> 00:22:21,828
There are so many places to dig into.

364
00:22:21,828 --> 00:22:24,649
These guys are real punks.
Makes me want to catch them even more.

365
00:22:25,496 --> 00:22:29,300
Find out if there were any other
missing persons reports around Mount Taegong.

366
00:22:29,300 --> 00:22:31,116
Also search the database

367
00:22:31,116 --> 00:22:33,952
to see if there have been any similar
unidentified bodies recently.

368
00:22:33,952 --> 00:22:36,124
What? Why is that?

369
00:22:36,124 --> 00:22:38,236
Someone who went missing in Gangwon Province

370
00:22:38,236 --> 00:22:40,749
was found buried in Seoul.

371
00:22:40,749 --> 00:22:45,449
They wouldn't go to that much trouble
just to dispose of one person.

372
00:22:48,992 --> 00:22:50,772
Hey, Beom. Go wait in the car first.

373
00:22:50,772 --> 00:22:52,316
I need to stop by somewhere.

374
00:22:52,316 --> 00:22:54,016
Okay.

375
00:22:56,508 --> 00:22:58,208
Come on! Let's do this!

376
00:23:00,788 --> 00:23:03,116
- Did you send it?
- Yeah, of course.

377
00:23:15,876 --> 00:23:17,576
Oh, dear.

378
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:22,224
Director Yoo Bo Na, good morning.

379
00:23:22,224 --> 00:23:24,417
Yeah, Ms. Oh Hyun Nam.

380
00:23:24,417 --> 00:23:26,583
- You are here?
- Yeah.

381
00:23:27,808 --> 00:23:29,668
Let's see.

382
00:23:29,668 --> 00:23:33,180
Oh, my, four people were added today.

383
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:37,049
Black, Gray, and Gold...

384
00:23:39,249 --> 00:23:43,816
We even have a White
for the first time in a while.

385
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:51,824
Alright.

386
00:23:51,824 --> 00:23:56,528
We have a new client list,
so let's have a productive meeting.

387
00:23:56,528 --> 00:23:57,796
Yes!

388
00:23:57,796 --> 00:23:59,644
Oh, seriously...

389
00:23:59,644 --> 00:24:02,696
Someone go and bring Manager Bong Tae Min.

390
00:24:02,696 --> 00:24:06,804
Wow, this client is a bit much.

391
00:24:06,804 --> 00:24:08,164
They're not going to be easy.

392
00:24:08,164 --> 00:24:10,944
Jeez, this month is going to be rough.

393
00:24:10,944 --> 00:24:12,296
I'll go get him.

394
00:24:12,296 --> 00:24:14,164
I'll...

395
00:24:14,164 --> 00:24:16,349
I'll go.

396
00:24:17,812 --> 00:24:21,849
That room is pretty nasty. Will she be okay?

397
00:24:21,849 --> 00:24:23,684
I should've given her a mask.

398
00:24:23,684 --> 00:24:27,588
She's used to all kinds of chemicals.

399
00:24:27,588 --> 00:24:29,549
She might actually enjoy it.

400
00:24:30,827 --> 00:24:33,583
Three, two...

401
00:24:36,611 --> 00:24:37,820
Darn it.

402
00:24:53,216 --> 00:24:55,572
<i>This was done by a top-level expert.</i>

403
00:24:55,572 --> 00:24:59,020
<i>You could call it genius-level work.</i>

404
00:24:59,020 --> 00:25:00,232
I looked into it.

405
00:25:00,232 --> 00:25:03,416
As expected, there are no guns
that use this kind of ammunition in Korea,

406
00:25:03,416 --> 00:25:06,016
and I couldn't find any overseas either.

407
00:25:06,016 --> 00:25:10,683
Then someone must have custom-made it.

408
00:25:10,683 --> 00:25:12,783
It was like that from the very first case.

409
00:25:12,783 --> 00:25:15,756
I asked because it seemed like
the bullets had changed this time.

410
00:25:15,756 --> 00:25:19,060
Meaning they upgrade
their equipment every few years.

411
00:25:19,060 --> 00:25:21,436
But if there's
a special top-tier technician like that,

412
00:25:21,436 --> 00:25:23,244
there's no way I wouldn't know.

413
00:25:23,244 --> 00:25:26,192
Does Kingfisher make the weapons themselves?

414
00:25:26,192 --> 00:25:28,068
Probably not. Making them personally...

415
00:25:28,068 --> 00:25:30,283
Well, considering what era we live in,

416
00:25:30,283 --> 00:25:33,716
they probably have
one or two capable assistants.

417
00:25:33,716 --> 00:25:37,516
Well, it could be one or two people,
or it could be an entire team.

418
00:25:37,516 --> 00:25:42,149
They could all be top-tier experts
like you said.

419
00:25:48,300 --> 00:25:50,216
And rice noodles?

420
00:25:54,980 --> 00:25:56,628
<i>Don't get in.</i>

421
00:25:56,628 --> 00:25:57,849
<i>Don't get in.</i>

422
00:25:57,849 --> 00:25:58,916
<i>Don't get in.</i>

423
00:25:58,916 --> 00:26:01,388
- <i>Don't get in.</i>
- <i>Please don't get in.</i>

424
00:26:01,388 --> 00:26:02,736
<i>Oh, that sly punk.</i>

425
00:26:02,736 --> 00:26:04,949
It's spacious, so let's get in.

426
00:26:07,120 --> 00:26:08,816
- Excuse me.
- We'll get in.

427
00:26:08,816 --> 00:26:11,483
- We'll get in.
- Thank you.

428
00:26:19,784 --> 00:26:21,152
I see a new face, huh?

429
00:26:21,152 --> 00:26:25,604
Oh, our Team 3 rookie.

430
00:26:25,604 --> 00:26:28,548
Oh, the one who just joined?

431
00:26:28,548 --> 00:26:30,868
Oh, dear, she's got bad luck.

432
00:26:30,868 --> 00:26:33,900
For a salesperson, where you start matters.

433
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:35,636
Well, but the timing works out.

434
00:26:35,636 --> 00:26:38,349
You know the whole sales team workshop
is scheduled, right?

435
00:26:38,349 --> 00:26:40,456
Mr. Bong, please take care of it.

436
00:26:40,456 --> 00:26:43,272
Yeah, of course.

437
00:26:43,272 --> 00:26:46,412
Well, adding more people doesn't
automatically improve results.

438
00:26:46,412 --> 00:26:49,668
A small elite team
with the right skills is enough.

439
00:26:49,668 --> 00:26:52,720
A sales technique that silently penetrates,
strikes once, and withdraws.

440
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:55,783
A true one-shot, one-kill move.

441
00:26:58,284 --> 00:27:01,116
Maybe I should set a date
and give them a special lecture sometime.

442
00:27:01,116 --> 00:27:03,649
- Exactly.
- Enjoy lunch.

443
00:27:08,300 --> 00:27:10,116
That punk...

444
00:27:13,680 --> 00:27:15,716
Let's go eat.

445
00:27:16,972 --> 00:27:18,672
Alright.

446
00:27:21,483 --> 00:27:23,156
This is so great, man.

447
00:27:23,156 --> 00:27:24,392
A three-tier cake.

448
00:27:24,392 --> 00:27:26,183
Oh, I'll prepare that.

449
00:27:26,183 --> 00:27:27,488
Oh, as expected.

450
00:27:27,488 --> 00:27:29,183
I'll definitely prepare a three-tier cake.

451
00:27:29,183 --> 00:27:31,853
Hyun Nam, try to understand.

452
00:27:31,853 --> 00:27:36,516
In sales, performance is
your rank and status.

453
00:27:36,516 --> 00:27:41,292
It must be hard navigating work-life, right?

454
00:27:41,292 --> 00:27:43,144
Speaking of which, Team Leader,

455
00:27:43,144 --> 00:27:47,416
since the results are fake anyway,
do we have to rank last every single time?

456
00:27:47,416 --> 00:27:50,752
I mean, not first place,
but maybe third place once in a while...

457
00:27:50,752 --> 00:27:52,860
Come on!

458
00:27:52,860 --> 00:27:56,588
There are so many people working
their feet off to sell even one more fan.

459
00:27:56,588 --> 00:27:59,509
It's right that we stay at the bottom.

460
00:27:59,509 --> 00:28:03,949
We can't hurt the people who work hard
and give it their all every day.

461
00:28:04,916 --> 00:28:08,276
Alright, then next month
we'll go below each team's

462
00:28:08,276 --> 00:28:10,749
lowest numbers again.

463
00:28:14,258 --> 00:28:17,268
But do we really have to go to a workshop?

464
00:28:17,268 --> 00:28:19,249
Isn't that a bit much?

465
00:28:19,249 --> 00:28:20,499
Normally, we wouldn't.

466
00:28:20,499 --> 00:28:24,384
We don't usually go,
but since you just joined,

467
00:28:24,384 --> 00:28:26,812
it feels awkward to skip it this time.

468
00:28:26,812 --> 00:28:28,676
It seems like a good opportunity to bond

469
00:28:28,676 --> 00:28:30,684
and get some fresh air together
after a long time.

470
00:28:30,684 --> 00:28:33,583
Don't you know a workshop
is still part of work?

471
00:28:36,608 --> 00:28:39,983
What could you even talk about
with people who sell fans?

472
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:44,568
Sounds fun. I've never been to one before.

473
00:28:44,568 --> 00:28:46,684
Wow, I'm excited.

474
00:28:46,684 --> 00:28:48,649
I can't wait to go.

475
00:28:54,148 --> 00:28:57,200
But Director Yoo, are you okay with it?
It's an overnight trip.

476
00:28:57,200 --> 00:28:58,900
Yeah.

477
00:28:59,920 --> 00:29:02,783
Go Blue Team!

478
00:29:02,783 --> 00:29:04,912
Wow, Team Leader,
you actually look pretty good in that.

479
00:29:04,912 --> 00:29:07,208
Really? I did put some effort in
since we're going to a workshop.

480
00:29:07,208 --> 00:29:08,948
Still, dressing alike like this
really makes it feel like

481
00:29:08,948 --> 00:29:11,049
we're going on a trip, right?

482
00:29:12,296 --> 00:29:14,140
<i>Mommy!</i>

483
00:29:14,140 --> 00:29:15,572
Yul!

484
00:29:15,572 --> 00:29:17,416
Wow, are you going to daycare now?

485
00:29:17,416 --> 00:29:18,416
<i>Yeah.</i>

486
00:29:18,416 --> 00:29:22,628
<i>Yul and Daddy are all ready
and heading out now!</i>

487
00:29:22,628 --> 00:29:24,984
<i>Go, go!</i>

488
00:29:24,984 --> 00:29:27,336
But are you really okay handling it alone?

489
00:29:27,336 --> 00:29:30,824
Should I ask Se Ah
to help out tonight, just in case?

490
00:29:30,824 --> 00:29:34,332
It's okay. I will be fine on my own.

491
00:29:34,332 --> 00:29:37,520
Don't worry and have fun.

492
00:29:37,520 --> 00:29:41,492
Okay, thank you. I will.

493
00:29:41,492 --> 00:29:45,483
Sweetie, want to say
"Have a good trip" to Mommy?

494
00:29:46,296 --> 00:29:47,928
When are you coming back?

495
00:29:47,928 --> 00:29:49,377
<i>Yul, that's not what we talked about.</i>

496
00:29:49,377 --> 00:29:53,872
I told you I'm only sleeping away
for one night, remember?

497
00:29:53,872 --> 00:29:55,104
Yeah, Yul!

498
00:29:55,104 --> 00:29:57,616
Can you be good with Daddy while I'm away?

499
00:29:57,616 --> 00:30:00,004
Where are you going?

500
00:30:00,004 --> 00:30:01,776
Well...

501
00:30:01,776 --> 00:30:03,296
<i>Wait a second.</i>

502
00:30:03,296 --> 00:30:05,536
<i>Yul, we have to do what we practiced.</i>

503
00:30:05,536 --> 00:30:08,549
<i>Sweetie, say goodbye to Mommy!</i>

504
00:30:09,216 --> 00:30:12,560
<i>Mommy, have a safe trip.</i>

505
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:14,184
<i>A vigorous salute!</i>

506
00:30:14,184 --> 00:30:16,016
<i>Hooah!</i>

507
00:30:16,836 --> 00:30:19,196
Hooah! I'll be back.

508
00:30:19,196 --> 00:30:21,283
Bye, Yul.

509
00:30:22,548 --> 00:30:25,816
Oh, no, she must feel terrible.

510
00:30:26,984 --> 00:30:30,783
It's probably the first time
being this far apart from her kid.

511
00:30:36,504 --> 00:30:37,516
Yes!

512
