770
00:45:15,998 --> 00:45:18,352
Oh, please have some of this.

771
00:45:18,352 --> 00:45:21,716
This honey water is the best
when your stomach hurts after drinking.

772
00:45:21,716 --> 00:45:23,283
- Oh, thank you.
- Thank you!

773
00:45:23,283 --> 00:45:24,883
- Thank you.
- Have a glass each.

774
00:45:24,883 --> 00:45:26,283
- Drink it all.
- Let me try.

775
00:45:26,283 --> 00:45:28,428
Excuse me, Ma'am. Just a moment.

776
00:45:28,428 --> 00:45:32,537
Which one did you put the most honey in?

777
00:45:32,537 --> 00:45:33,936
- Oh, dear.
- Is it this one?

778
00:45:33,936 --> 00:45:36,649
I'll take this one.

779
00:45:37,475 --> 00:45:40,062
Then I'll...

780
00:45:40,062 --> 00:45:42,449
- Maybe this one has more?
- Yes, go ahead.

781
00:45:43,052 --> 00:45:44,842
I'll have this one.

782
00:45:44,842 --> 00:45:46,410
- Yeah.
- Go ahead.

783
00:45:46,410 --> 00:45:47,416
Thank you for the drink.

784
00:45:47,416 --> 00:45:49,416
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

785
00:45:49,416 --> 00:45:52,100
- Thank you.
- Try this one.

786
00:45:52,100 --> 00:45:55,356
This is natural honey.

787
00:45:55,356 --> 00:45:57,172
Thank you so much for the honey water.

788
00:45:57,172 --> 00:45:58,404
Oh, yeah.

789
00:45:58,404 --> 00:46:03,983
- Bottoms up!
- Bottoms up!

790
00:46:07,910 --> 00:46:09,610
Thank you.

791
00:46:10,460 --> 00:46:14,116
- It's really sweet.
- Then enjoy yourselves.

792
00:46:14,116 --> 00:46:16,572
- Oh, yeah.
- Yes.

793
00:46:16,572 --> 00:46:18,272
Keep drinking.

794
00:46:19,257 --> 00:46:20,983
Yeah, got it.

795
00:46:35,952 --> 00:46:38,216
These punks are crossing the line.

796
00:46:41,128 --> 00:46:42,540
[Mount Taegong Missing Persons Map]
Their hideout is believed to be

797
00:46:42,540 --> 00:46:47,749
Taegong Grandpa Pension
on the east side of Mount Taegong.

798
00:46:55,656 --> 00:47:00,248
But we still don't have any solid evidence.

799
00:47:00,248 --> 00:47:03,483
You know the whole sales team workshop
is scheduled, right?

800
00:47:03,483 --> 00:47:05,387
Mr. Bong, please take care of it.

801
00:47:05,387 --> 00:47:08,149
Yeah, of course.

802
00:47:11,424 --> 00:47:13,316
Let's go!

803
00:47:16,032 --> 00:47:17,124
Remember,

804
00:47:17,124 --> 00:47:21,028
the goal is gathering information,
not a meeting.

805
00:47:21,028 --> 00:47:24,460
And remember, their safety comes first.

806
00:47:24,460 --> 00:47:26,160
Yes!

807
00:47:43,516 --> 00:47:44,860
The entire exterior of the building

808
00:47:44,860 --> 00:47:46,929
is equipped with electromagnetic
shielding devices.

809
00:47:46,929 --> 00:47:49,949
It seems designed to cut off communication
with the outside in case of an emergency.

810
00:48:38,892 --> 00:48:41,144
- Bingo!
- Excuse me, Ma'am.

811
00:48:41,144 --> 00:48:46,166
Which one did you put the most honey in?

812
00:48:46,166 --> 00:48:47,391
It's not dangerous.

813
00:48:47,391 --> 00:48:48,640
It's just a sleeping pill.

814
00:48:48,640 --> 00:48:51,083
I'll have this one.

815
00:48:52,248 --> 00:48:54,149
It's an antidote.

816
00:48:57,121 --> 00:49:00,508
They've never gone after guests before.

817
00:49:00,508 --> 00:49:02,040
They must have lost their minds.

818
00:49:02,040 --> 00:49:06,440
Now that the police are onto them,
they're trying to make one big score and run.

819
00:49:06,440 --> 00:49:08,304
We'll keep monitoring the situation for now.

820
00:49:08,304 --> 00:49:10,228
By the way, I haven't seen
Tae Min for a while.

821
00:49:10,228 --> 00:49:12,449
Assistant Manager Ki went out
because his communication wasn't working.

822
00:49:12,449 --> 00:49:14,201
The phones are dead too.

823
00:49:14,201 --> 00:49:16,068
They must have activated the device.

824
00:49:16,068 --> 00:49:17,958
Darn it.

825
00:49:17,958 --> 00:49:19,816
I'll go find him.

826
00:49:23,584 --> 00:49:25,776
Please look after Director Yoo.

827
00:49:25,776 --> 00:49:27,549
Got it. So hurry back.

828
00:49:35,824 --> 00:49:37,972
Assistant Manager Ki!

829
00:49:37,972 --> 00:49:40,116
Manager Tae Min!

830
00:49:40,748 --> 00:49:43,016
Where are they?

831
00:49:44,416 --> 00:49:46,504
Assistant Manager Ki!

832
00:49:46,504 --> 00:49:48,716
Manager Tae Min!

833
00:50:06,856 --> 00:50:08,556
Oh, seriously.

834
00:50:15,990 --> 00:50:18,316
What's that in their hands?

835
00:50:23,132 --> 00:50:25,332
Wow, how much is all this?

836
00:50:25,332 --> 00:50:28,457
We hit the jackpot today.

837
00:50:28,457 --> 00:50:30,102
Tie them all up!

838
00:50:30,102 --> 00:50:31,949
Yes!

839
00:50:32,916 --> 00:50:36,844
It's actually better that they passed out
from the sleeping pills.

840
00:50:36,844 --> 00:50:38,716
Jeez, crazy punks.

841
00:50:38,716 --> 00:50:42,283
Forget those lunatics for now.
Let's find Assistant Manager Ki first.

842
00:50:42,283 --> 00:50:45,383
His comms have been dead for a while.
Looks like they got him.

843
00:50:46,749 --> 00:50:48,749
Think he's already dead?

844
00:50:48,749 --> 00:50:50,483
Excuse me.

845
00:50:51,720 --> 00:50:54,124
If he's alive, he has to be
somewhere around here.

846
00:50:54,124 --> 00:50:56,516
No cars have left the property.

847
00:51:04,460 --> 00:51:06,583
Tie them up tight.

848
00:51:06,583 --> 00:51:10,416
Hey, move your head, jeez.

849
00:51:15,430 --> 00:51:16,928
What's with these people?

850
00:51:16,928 --> 00:51:18,240
Why are they still awake?

851
00:51:18,240 --> 00:51:19,972
Hey, folks.

852
00:51:19,972 --> 00:51:23,983
If you keep this up, things are
going to get difficult for you.

853
00:51:26,000 --> 00:51:28,549
Wow, listen to me talking.

854
00:51:29,600 --> 00:51:30,676
Old man!

855
00:51:30,676 --> 00:51:33,768
Some of them are still awake.
What do we do? Kill them?

856
00:51:33,768 --> 00:51:35,583
Are you insane?

857
00:51:38,761 --> 00:51:40,690
They're worth 300 million won each.

858
00:51:40,690 --> 00:51:42,390
300 million won.

859
00:51:45,704 --> 00:51:49,293
That old hag got distracted again.

860
00:51:49,293 --> 00:51:50,852
Just tie them up for now.

861
00:51:50,852 --> 00:51:52,716
Or knock them out.

862
00:51:52,716 --> 00:51:55,340
How exactly do you knock someone out?

863
00:51:55,340 --> 00:51:57,576
I don't want to be hurt.

864
00:51:57,576 --> 00:52:00,216
Darn, my phone's dead again.

865
00:52:00,216 --> 00:52:01,736
That's a problem, isn't it?

866
00:52:01,736 --> 00:52:05,116
What? You're going to call the cops?

867
00:52:05,116 --> 00:52:07,283
- Give me a break.
- Come on.

868
00:52:07,283 --> 00:52:10,516
Friend, don't be like that.
Let's just talk this out...

869
00:52:11,716 --> 00:52:12,783
- Team Leader!
- Team Leader!

870
00:52:12,783 --> 00:52:13,876
We'll communicate physically.

871
00:52:13,876 --> 00:52:17,049
- You punks...
- My fists have been itching anyway.

872
00:52:17,049 --> 00:52:18,983
Don't rush your death.

873
00:52:18,983 --> 00:52:20,249
Hey, just keep your mouth shut.

874
00:52:20,249 --> 00:52:21,316
Knife! Knife! Knife!

875
00:52:21,316 --> 00:52:23,683
Please save me.

876
00:52:23,683 --> 00:52:25,583
Please save me!

877
00:52:26,549 --> 00:52:29,260
- Team Leader!
- There's a girl over there.

878
00:52:29,260 --> 00:52:31,883
Go tie her up.
Tie up everyone over there and here.

879
00:52:34,701 --> 00:52:36,320
You're going to regret this.

880
00:52:36,320 --> 00:52:37,340
We'll regret it?

881
00:52:37,340 --> 00:52:38,340
Team Leader?

882
00:52:38,340 --> 00:52:40,383
Put that down.

883
00:52:46,010 --> 00:52:48,412
<i>Your call cannot be connected
and is being forwarded to voicemail.</i>

884
00:52:48,412 --> 00:52:49,824
<i>After the beep...</i>

885
00:52:52,100 --> 00:52:54,942
What should we do?
Mommy keeps not answering her phone.

886
00:52:54,942 --> 00:52:58,256
I miss mommy.

887
00:52:58,256 --> 00:52:59,993
You miss mommy?

888
00:52:59,993 --> 00:53:03,368
I miss Mommy a lot too.

889
00:53:03,368 --> 00:53:05,520
Why isn't Mommy answering?

890
00:53:05,520 --> 00:53:09,016
Mommy is deep in the woods right now.

891
00:53:09,016 --> 00:53:10,890
So the phone signal isn't good there.

892
00:53:10,890 --> 00:53:12,100
In the woods?

893
00:53:12,100 --> 00:53:17,641
Then what if Mommy meets a wolf
like Little Red Riding Hood?

894
00:53:17,641 --> 00:53:19,341
What?

895
00:53:20,781 --> 00:53:22,449
Is it here?

896
00:53:22,449 --> 00:53:24,783
It's locked. What do we do?

897
00:53:32,643 --> 00:53:34,343
Wow...

898
00:53:55,636 --> 00:53:58,316
Assistant Manager Ki, are you in there?

899
00:53:59,784 --> 00:54:01,484
Hey!

900
00:54:09,028 --> 00:54:11,149
Here, here!

901
00:54:14,349 --> 00:54:17,003
Hurry, hurry.

902
00:54:17,003 --> 00:54:20,616
What a surprise. Our Assistant Manager Ki
has gone missing in action again?

903
00:54:23,916 --> 00:54:26,064
You really never disappoint.

904
00:54:26,064 --> 00:54:29,816
Isn't it proper to be surprised
and worried at a time like this?

905
00:54:29,816 --> 00:54:32,483
Oh, my, what do we do? Are you okay?

906
00:54:33,290 --> 00:54:35,216
Do you two not get along?

907
00:54:36,149 --> 00:54:39,180
Well, how awful.

908
00:54:39,180 --> 00:54:40,180
What's it like in there?

909
00:54:40,180 --> 00:54:42,052
They've already stormed in.

910
00:54:42,052 --> 00:54:43,249
There are quite a few of them.

911
00:54:43,249 --> 00:54:44,458
Looks like they planned this.

912
00:54:44,458 --> 00:54:46,136
Shouldn't we hurry and go?

913
00:54:46,136 --> 00:54:47,983
They've probably already started fighting.

914
00:54:47,983 --> 00:54:49,683
Yeah.

915
00:54:50,580 --> 00:54:52,280
Yeah.

916
00:54:54,031 --> 00:54:57,075
Team Leader!

917
00:54:57,075 --> 00:55:00,016
- I won't let you go, you punks.
- Ouch!

918
00:55:02,696 --> 00:55:04,693
Can't we touch them? Why?

919
00:55:04,693 --> 00:55:06,241
They're gray.

920
00:55:06,241 --> 00:55:09,883
- What?
- They're not approved for a meeting yet.

921
00:55:09,883 --> 00:55:12,006
Gray means they're still under investigation,
not confirmed clients.

922
00:55:12,006 --> 00:55:13,624
Don't you know that?

923
00:55:13,624 --> 00:55:15,736
I know that much.

924
00:55:15,736 --> 00:55:18,083
But they attacked us first!

925
00:55:18,083 --> 00:55:23,483
Under no circumstances
do we conduct a meeting with a non-client.

926
00:55:23,483 --> 00:55:25,565
We only deal with targets

927
00:55:25,565 --> 00:55:28,172
that have been verified multiple times

928
00:55:28,172 --> 00:55:32,016
and finally approved through the system.

929
00:55:32,016 --> 00:55:34,149
That's our rule.

930
00:55:35,440 --> 00:55:36,849
So we're just supposed to
sit here and take it?

931
00:55:36,849 --> 00:55:38,765
There are other people in there too.

932
00:55:38,765 --> 00:55:42,016
Don't worry so much. I said it's not yet.

933
00:55:43,213 --> 00:55:44,949
Tie them up tight.

934
00:55:44,949 --> 00:55:47,316
Hurry up.

935
00:55:47,316 --> 00:55:49,416
Do it properly.

936
00:55:53,560 --> 00:55:55,883
Team Leader, are you okay?

937
00:55:57,313 --> 00:55:59,664
I'm fine.

938
00:55:59,664 --> 00:56:03,348
They wouldn't actually kill us, would they?

939
00:56:03,348 --> 00:56:04,348
We will.

940
00:56:04,348 --> 00:56:06,524
Oh, yeah?

941
00:56:06,524 --> 00:56:07,616
And how are you planning to do that?

942
00:56:07,616 --> 00:56:09,896
How would you like to die?

943
00:56:09,896 --> 00:56:11,816
Should I specially cut your belly open
while you're alive?

944
00:56:11,816 --> 00:56:12,883
Come on.

945
00:56:12,883 --> 00:56:14,680
- Oh.
- No.

946
00:56:14,680 --> 00:56:17,883
Since your eyes are so sparkly,
I should gouge those out first.

947
00:56:17,883 --> 00:56:19,449
They still look like they're worth something.

948
00:56:19,449 --> 00:56:23,200
That's right. I've got the best eyesight.

949
00:56:23,200 --> 00:56:24,964
I've eaten a lot of lettuce.

950
00:56:24,964 --> 00:56:26,916
Beta-carotene, you know.

951
00:56:27,728 --> 00:56:29,536
B-B-Beta what?

952
00:56:29,536 --> 00:56:32,183
Beta-carotene, you moron.

953
00:56:33,149 --> 00:56:35,016
Why are you even entertaining his nonsense?

954
00:56:35,016 --> 00:56:37,308
Stop the nonsense and move them
to the warehouse quickly.

955
00:56:37,308 --> 00:56:41,540
And call Dr. Jo to come in
early in the morning!

956
00:56:41,540 --> 00:56:43,883
Contact all the clients.

957
00:56:45,681 --> 00:56:48,171
They'll love this.

958
00:56:48,171 --> 00:56:51,349
They're all young and healthy.

959
00:56:52,428 --> 00:56:54,680
I think we're really going to die.
What do we do?

960
00:56:54,680 --> 00:56:56,491
Oh, don't worry.

961
00:56:56,491 --> 00:57:00,852
My fortune says I'll live to 150.

962
00:57:00,852 --> 00:57:02,356
You're full of it.

963
00:57:02,356 --> 00:57:05,828
Hey, you punk, what have you been
staring at so intently?

964
00:57:05,828 --> 00:57:08,000
The phone, idiot. That phone.

965
00:57:08,000 --> 00:57:10,916
The phone doesn't even work. Darn it!

966
00:57:13,649 --> 00:57:15,349
What?

967
00:57:16,732 --> 00:57:17,858
Huh? What is it?

968
00:57:23,880 --> 00:57:26,283
[Emergency Notice]
"Pre-meeting with the client approved"?

969
00:57:26,283 --> 00:57:27,283
What is this?

970
00:57:27,283 --> 00:57:29,483
Looks like we finally got approval.

971
00:57:34,716 --> 00:57:38,716
Alright, let's slowly start our meeting.

972
00:57:43,372 --> 00:57:46,316
It's done. We've arrived.

973
00:57:46,316 --> 00:57:48,015
Found it.

974
00:57:48,015 --> 00:57:49,388
<i>I've sent the evidence.</i>

975
00:57:49,388 --> 00:57:51,436
<i>Requesting emergency meeting approval.</i>

976
00:57:51,436 --> 00:57:52,616
So what do we do now?

977
00:57:52,616 --> 00:57:56,281
They're heavily armed.
What if it comes down to hand-to-hand combat?

978
00:57:56,281 --> 00:57:58,116
You're worrying for nothing again.

979
00:58:03,248 --> 00:58:06,344
<i>Team leader served
in the Army Special Forces.</i>

980
00:58:06,344 --> 00:58:09,083
<i>He's especially skilled
in close-quarters combat.</i>

981
00:58:10,964 --> 00:58:13,028
Oh, my.

982
00:58:13,028 --> 00:58:15,464
<i>Assistant Manager Yang's hobby
is every combat sport imaginable.</i>

983
00:58:15,464 --> 00:58:18,516
<i>Judo, taekwondo, kickboxing...</i>

984
00:58:18,516 --> 00:58:20,616
<i>There's nothing she can't do.</i>

985
00:58:26,620 --> 00:58:28,320
Jeez.

986
00:58:31,592 --> 00:58:34,483
You are all bark and no bite.

987
00:58:36,060 --> 00:58:37,956
Director!

988
00:58:37,956 --> 00:58:39,656
Director!

989
00:58:45,392 --> 00:58:48,249
Hands up, you punk!

990
00:58:49,972 --> 00:58:51,672
Oh, dear.

991
00:58:52,906 --> 00:58:55,149
An elderly person like you...

992
00:58:55,798 --> 00:59:00,849
shouldn't be playing
with dangerous things like this.

993
00:59:01,743 --> 00:59:03,779
Oh, that's hot!

994
00:59:03,779 --> 00:59:08,049
Shut up! Face the wall,
and put your hands up.

995
00:59:09,818 --> 00:59:11,583
Hurry!

996
00:59:16,499 --> 00:59:18,199
The rest of you too!

997
00:59:20,776 --> 00:59:23,149
Hey, move them against the wall!

998
00:59:25,664 --> 00:59:26,816
Team Leader!

999
00:59:26,816 --> 00:59:29,583
Hey, step on him.

1000
00:59:32,616 --> 00:59:34,975
Hey, hey!

1001
00:59:34,975 --> 00:59:37,549
If possible, don't touch the stomach area.

1002
00:59:37,549 --> 00:59:40,783
- It's 300 million won each!
- Yes!

1003
00:59:46,712 --> 00:59:50,864
<i>Then what if a wolf shows up
while Mommy's in the woods?</i>

1004
00:59:50,864 --> 00:59:53,158
The wolf would be too scared and run away.

1005
00:59:53,158 --> 00:59:55,452
Mommy's stronger than the wolf?

1006
00:59:55,452 --> 00:59:59,583
Of course, Mommy is much stronger.
Mommy's super strong.

1007
00:59:59,583 --> 01:00:04,036
She can climb the roughest
mountain trails like it's nothing.

1008
01:00:04,036 --> 01:00:09,046
Even through deep snow,
she plows a path like a bulldozer.

1009
01:00:09,046 --> 01:00:12,784
She's so strong
that she can lift me with ease.

1010
01:00:12,784 --> 01:00:16,749
Well... And...

1011
01:00:18,872 --> 01:00:22,249
She's really fearless...

1012
01:00:26,800 --> 01:00:28,737
The Mommy I know

1013
01:00:28,737 --> 01:00:33,344
is a wonderful person
who is rough and strong,

1014
01:00:33,344 --> 01:00:35,549
yet never loses her grace.

1015
01:00:36,616 --> 01:00:38,420
What is it?

1016
01:00:38,420 --> 01:00:40,883
Why's it so darn noisy?

1017
01:00:42,268 --> 01:00:44,249
Well.

1018
01:00:47,896 --> 01:00:49,872
Director Yoo is awake.

1019
01:00:49,872 --> 01:00:51,192
Director Yoo.

1020
01:00:51,192 --> 01:00:54,040
Oh, darn it, who is it? You noisy punks.

1021
01:00:54,040 --> 01:00:55,956
I can't sleep.

1022
01:00:55,956 --> 01:00:57,552
What's this? Who did this?

1023
01:00:57,552 --> 01:00:59,383
Who tied me up like this?

1024
01:00:59,383 --> 01:01:03,498
- Was it you?
- What's with that woman?

1025
01:01:03,498 --> 01:01:07,183
Where did all these darn flies come from?

1026
01:01:07,183 --> 01:01:08,549
What? Flies?

1027
01:01:08,549 --> 01:01:10,883
Flies? You crazy punk!

1028
01:01:15,816 --> 01:01:18,749
You said you could handle it alone.
Did you get old already? Huh?

1029
01:01:18,749 --> 01:01:21,324
Well, I've been at it for months.

1030
01:01:21,324 --> 01:01:23,716
I figured I'd at least try doing it myself.

1031
01:01:23,716 --> 01:01:26,241
It was your first outing in a while.

1032
01:01:26,241 --> 01:01:30,208
I wanted you to drink, sleep well,
and enjoy yourself.

1033
01:01:30,208 --> 01:01:35,252
Then this old geezer suddenly
showed up with a gun.

1034
01:01:35,252 --> 01:01:36,480
- A gun?
- Yeah.

1035
01:01:36,480 --> 01:01:38,449
He's got a gun?

1036
01:01:39,508 --> 01:01:42,196
Director Yoo, take care of this.

1037
01:01:42,196 --> 01:01:44,916
Move, you punks.

1038
01:01:47,272 --> 01:01:49,207
Hey!

1039
01:01:49,207 --> 01:01:50,900
You, kneel.

1040
01:01:50,900 --> 01:01:52,556
Yeah, kneel.

1041
01:01:52,556 --> 01:01:53,849
Get on your knees, you punk!

1042
01:01:53,849 --> 01:01:56,816
Where'd this old fly come buzzing from?

1043
01:01:57,908 --> 01:01:59,735
That punk...

1044
01:01:59,735 --> 01:02:02,449
You want a hole in your head?

1045
01:02:03,548 --> 01:02:05,207
"A hole in your head"?

1046
01:02:05,207 --> 01:02:06,907
That's my line.

1047
01:02:08,207 --> 01:02:09,960
Oh, jeez, I...

1048
01:02:09,960 --> 01:02:14,311
Don't move! Move, and I'll shoot!

1049
01:02:14,311 --> 01:02:16,416
If I move, you won't be able to hit me.

1050
01:02:17,816 --> 01:02:21,964
Seriously... Has she lost her mind?

1051
01:02:21,964 --> 01:02:24,583
Go ahead. I'm staying still here.

1052
01:02:28,083 --> 01:02:29,864
T-T-That's right.

1053
01:02:29,864 --> 01:02:31,849
Die, you punk!

1054
01:02:33,949 --> 01:02:36,283
Old man!

1055
01:02:36,283 --> 01:02:39,749
- Old man.
- You couldn't even shoot me?

1056
01:02:42,791 --> 01:02:44,616
I won't shoot. I won't.

1057
01:02:44,616 --> 01:02:46,316
You won't shoot?

1058
01:02:53,116 --> 01:02:54,286
Time to go.

1059
01:02:54,286 --> 01:02:56,072
Hey! Kill that punk!

1060
01:02:56,072 --> 01:02:57,652
Shall I go for it after a long time?

1061
01:02:57,652 --> 01:02:59,516
Come at me all at once, you flies!

1062
01:02:59,516 --> 01:03:01,516
Hey! Kill that punk!

1063
01:03:04,549 --> 01:03:06,803
Missed.

1064
01:03:06,803 --> 01:03:08,583
Guess I'll just go then.

1065
01:03:09,549 --> 01:03:11,316
Hey, you punk!

1066
01:03:33,504 --> 01:03:35,816
Yoo Bo Na's drunk habit is out.

1067
01:03:38,168 --> 01:03:39,868
Bo Na...

1068
01:03:50,428 --> 01:03:52,849
Why do you keep getting up?

1069
01:04:06,575 --> 01:04:08,849
<i>A woman as agile as a puma,</i>

1070
01:04:08,849 --> 01:04:10,974
<i>as mighty as a lion,</i>

1071
01:04:10,974 --> 01:04:13,564
<i>and as graceful as a swan.</i>

1072
01:04:13,564 --> 01:04:15,516
<i>Yoo Bo Na looked</i>

1073
01:04:16,372 --> 01:04:18,749
truly beautiful then.

1074
01:04:53,649 --> 01:04:55,549
Get on your knees, you punk!

1075
01:05:02,149 --> 01:05:04,883
Director Yoo's still got it!

1076
01:05:40,662 --> 01:05:43,819
Yul, I told you I have to
go to work today, so I can't, right?

1077
01:05:43,819 --> 01:05:44,824
I hate you, Mommy.

1078
01:05:44,824 --> 01:05:46,740
So this guy is getting out after all?

1079
01:05:46,740 --> 01:05:48,764
But we should move up the timeline.

1080
01:05:48,764 --> 01:05:50,311
Before he returns to his neighborhood.

1081
01:05:50,311 --> 01:05:51,932
That'll cause quite a stir.

1082
01:05:51,932 --> 01:05:53,968
He died the day he was released.

1083
01:05:53,968 --> 01:05:56,349
What if we followed the crimes
before they happen?

1084
01:05:56,349 --> 01:05:58,564
Sir, welcome.

1085
01:05:58,564 --> 01:06:00,152
Kingfisher's next target.

1086
01:06:00,152 --> 01:06:01,583
Is this connected to Kingfisher?

1087
01:06:01,583 --> 01:06:03,816
Were you following me?

1088
01:06:03,816 --> 01:06:05,168
What's going on? Team Leader!

1089
01:06:05,168 --> 01:06:07,949
I'm Pyo Kyu Cheol, you punks!

1090
01:06:07,949 --> 01:06:10,960
That puts Director Yoo
in the most dangerous position.

1091
01:06:10,960 --> 01:06:13,516
She's also the most likely to get caught.
